1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,834
This is every level of American body armor, from a vest that stops a pistol to a plate that stops an armor-piercing rifle round.

2
00:00:09,067 --> 00:00:13,587
And one of the most popular levels you can buy does not officially exist.

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,173
Step one.

4
00:00:15,213 --> 00:00:16,123
Level Two A.

5
00:00:16,367 --> 00:00:18,531
The thinnest armor on the list.

6
00:00:18,571 --> 00:00:22,442
A soft, flexible vest, made from layers of woven fiber.

7
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:28,808
It was tested against a nine millimeter bullet traveling at 1,225 feet per second.

8
00:00:29,033 --> 00:00:31,467
And in the newest standard, it is gone.

9
00:00:31,507 --> 00:00:33,687
Level Two A was dropped completely.

10
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,297
Step two.

11
00:00:35,337 --> 00:00:36,116
Level Two.

12
00:00:36,333 --> 00:00:42,003
Thicker, still soft, and rated for nine millimeter and .357 Magnum rounds.

13
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:45,550
Soft armor like this owes a lot to one man.

14
00:00:45,590 --> 00:00:55,543
In 1972, a pizza shop owner named Richard Davis knelt at a police range in Walled Lake, Michigan, and shot himself in the chest.

15
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,407
He was wearing his own vest.

16
00:00:57,447 --> 00:01:00,112
He stood up, and kept shooting at the targets.

17
00:01:00,367 --> 00:01:05,191
He went on to repeat that demonstration more than 190 times.

18
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:08,992
In the new system, Level Two is called H G one.

19
00:01:09,032 --> 00:01:10,293
H G, for handgun.

20
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:11,961
Step three.

21
00:01:12,001 --> 00:01:12,981
Level Three A.

22
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,604
The strongest soft armor there is.

23
00:01:15,644 --> 00:01:20,564
It adds the .44 Magnum, one of the most powerful handgun rounds made.

24
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:23,926
It is still something you can wear under a shirt.

25
00:01:23,966 --> 00:01:25,542
It is now called H G two.

26
00:01:25,767 --> 00:01:28,848
And no soft vest on this list will stop a rifle.

27
00:01:29,767 --> 00:01:31,875
Step four is not a level at all.

28
00:01:31,915 --> 00:01:34,560
It is the rule that decides every level.

29
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:36,965
Stopping the bullet is not enough.

30
00:01:37,005 --> 00:01:40,079
Behind the armor, testers place a block of clay.

31
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:44,437
When the bullet hits, the armor bends, and pushes a dent into that clay.

32
00:01:44,667 --> 00:01:53,743
If the dent is deeper than 44 millimeters, about an inch and three quarters, the armor fails, even if the bullet never got through.

33
00:01:54,633 --> 00:01:55,362
Step five.

34
00:01:55,402 --> 00:01:56,285
Level Three.

35
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:58,710
This is where soft armor ends.

36
00:01:58,750 --> 00:02:03,885
Level Three is a rigid plate, made of ceramic, steel or polyethylene.

37
00:02:04,133 --> 00:02:10,330
Its test round is the 7.62 NATO rifle bullet, at 2,780 feet per second.

38
00:02:10,370 --> 00:02:14,546
More than twice as fast as the Level Two A test.

39
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,890
The plate has to stop six of them.

40
00:02:17,133 --> 00:02:19,210
Its new name is R F one.

41
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:20,532
R F, for rifle.

42
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:22,089
Step six.

43
00:02:22,129 --> 00:02:23,404
Level Three plus.

44
00:02:23,633 --> 00:02:26,561
You will find it on armor websites everywhere.

45
00:02:26,601 --> 00:02:29,142
It is the level people argue about most.

46
00:02:29,367 --> 00:02:31,393
And it was never an official level.

47
00:02:31,433 --> 00:02:34,699
There is no Level Three plus in the government standard.

48
00:02:34,933 --> 00:02:42,293
Makers invented it to say their plates stop more than Level Three, usually the green-tipped 5.56 round.

49
00:02:42,333 --> 00:02:46,388
But what plus means changes from one company to the next.

50
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:48,363
Step seven.

51
00:02:48,403 --> 00:02:49,165
R F two.

52
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:52,217
So the newest standard did something about it.

53
00:02:52,257 --> 00:02:55,446
It created a brand new level between Three and Four.

54
00:02:55,700 --> 00:03:02,047
R F two must stop everything R F one does, plus the green-tipped 5.56 round.

55
00:03:02,087 --> 00:03:06,249
The gap that marketing filled now has a real name.

56
00:03:07,167 --> 00:03:07,934
Step eight.

57
00:03:07,974 --> 00:03:08,741
Level Four.

58
00:03:08,967 --> 00:03:10,457
The top of the ladder.

59
00:03:10,497 --> 00:03:15,951
Its test round is the .30-06 armor-piercing bullet, with a hardened steel core.

60
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:18,336
It is now called R F three.

61
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,359
So here is the whole ladder.

62
00:03:21,399 --> 00:03:22,559
Two A is gone.

63
00:03:22,599 --> 00:03:23,844
Two is H G one.

64
00:03:23,884 --> 00:03:25,472
Three A is H G two.

65
00:03:25,512 --> 00:03:26,929
Three is R F one.

66
00:03:26,969 --> 00:03:29,157
Three plus became R F two.

67
00:03:29,197 --> 00:03:31,042
And Four is R F three.

68
00:03:31,267 --> 00:03:37,115
The level that does not exist was so popular that the government finally had to make it real.

69
00:03:37,367 --> 00:03:39,601
Which level would you trust with your life?

70
00:03:39,641 --> 00:03:40,871
Tell me in the comments.
